{"conjecture": "Software systems accumulate an implicit constraint network—unseen invariants between distant modules that are never documented because no single change introduces them. Each locally correct change tightens this network by adding another implicit dependency, progressively shrinking the space of future valid changes. Engineers perceive this as increasing complexity not because the code grew, but because the ratio of enforced-but-invisible constraints to visible interfaces asymptotically approaches a state where most modifications violate an invariant they cannot see."}
